# ESP32 Conventions

## NVS namespaces — keep separate

| Namespace | Keys | File |
|-----------|------|------|
| `wifi` | `portal` (force setup screen) | `wifi_setup.cpp` |
| `radar` | `lat`, `lon` | `radar_location.cpp` |
| `planeradar` | `rangeIdx`, `useMiles`, `showRwys` | `radar_range.cpp` |

Do not merge namespaces or hold overlapping `Preferences` handles — code comments warn of conflicts.

## Main loop contract

- Call `wifiLoop()` every `loop()` iteration
- Long I/O must poll the network: ADS-B uses `services::adsb::setPollFn(wifiLoop)` during HTTP
- BOOT button (GPIO 9, active LOW): poll `bootButtonPollLongPress()` and consume taps via `bootButtonConsumeTap()` during blocking work

## Config and hardware

- Pins, SPI, WiFi timing, ADS-B interval → `include/config.h`
- Do not scatter magic GPIO numbers or timing constants in UI/service code

## Credential reset

Long BOOT hold (3 s) calls `wifiResetCredentialsAndReboot()` which clears WiFi, location (`services::location::clear()`), and units (`ui::radar::unitsReset()`). New persisted settings must join this wipe path.

## WiFi TX power

Both AP and STA modes use `WiFi.setTxPower(WIFI_POWER_8_5dBm)` in `wifi_setup.cpp`. Do not raise TX power without testing stability.
